## Frequently asked questions

### Will my agency know you are reviewing their work?

Only if you tell them. I use read-only access to your own Search Console and GA4 accounts. I read the reports you already hold. I do not contact your agency.

### Do you need logins to our website or the agency's tools?

No. Read-only Google Search Console and GA4 access is enough. Add the reports and contract you already have. I audit the public site with a crawler.

### Is this a sales pitch for your retainer?

No. The review is a fixed £495 piece of work with no obligation. I will say so and suggest you renew if the evidence shows your agency is doing well.

### Can you review a PPC or paid social agency?

No. I review SEO and AI-search work only. Ask a specialist in paid media for that channel.

### What if our site has more than 500 pages?

Larger sites, multiple international versions or a recent migration need a separate scope. I confirm this before any paid work starts.

### How far back do you look?

Search Console holds up to 16 months of performance data. I usually cover the full contract period where it fits inside that window. Older reports are still useful for checking what was promised.

